    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2156" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰγίλιψ</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[γῐ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐπος</span>, ὁ, ἡ,
		(expl. by Gramm. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αῐξ</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, λείπω</span>, cf. Sch. <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			9.15
		</span></i>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>destitute even of
			goats</i>, hence, <i>steep, sheer</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.15
				</span></i>
			, al. (not in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				794
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				1325
			</span></i>; also in form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰγίλιπος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (Perh. cognate with Lith.<i>lipti</i> `climb'.)</div>
